                    522.0,
                    710.0
                ],
                [
                    113.0,
                    710.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "L. The parties agree to participate in a joint Fringe Benefit Committee for the purpose of discussing current insurance coverages, reviewing alternatives to the current coverages and reviewing improvements in the current coverages. The committee shall be composed of representatives from the Association, representatives from the Board, and representatives from other recognized bargaining units within the District. This committee shall have no power or authority to agree to any changes in insurances that would require negotiations. Both parties agree that the Fringe Benefit Committee shall have the authority to submit proposed changes in the insurance package to the Supentendent or his designee for analysis of both program impact and cost. The parties may submit unlimited requests by mutual consent. Each party may submit up to three (3) additional requests. Requests shall be submitted by October 15 and responses provided to the Fringe Benefit Committee by February 15.",
